    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="0479" n="397" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg397"/>

                <head>Mr. Hunter to Mr.
                        Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 184.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 26, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch of the 13th instant, No. 117, transmitting a copy of your note of the
                    day before to Mr. Drouyn de Lhuys, correcting certain mistakes which had
                    occurred in representing what you had said and written in regard, respectively,
                    to the position of the United States as to the Mexican question and the
                    revocation to the French decree concerning so-called belligerent rights of the
                    insurgents.</p>
                <p>I am happy to inform you that your note is fully approved.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. HUNTER,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c., Paris.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
